From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] opengl: show the 3D video of an X11 window in 3D, each view at
 its own resolution, and say when the desktop does not take the declaration

On X11 (also through Xwayland) the video of the Qt interface is a child
window of the interface's window, and the video output declared that child
with stereo_declare_x11(), as if it were a top-level window. Stereo KWin
shows the two views of a child one for each eye only when its top-level
window lists it (_KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_CHILDREN, support version 5),
so the declaration was ignored and a 3D video showed one view in both eyes.

A 3D video is now drawn on a window of the video output's own, made inside
the video window before the OpenGL surface exists and left to the OpenGL
modules through the variable gl-x11-window (egl.c and glx.c draw on it, the
x11-window.h helper is theirs in common). The interface keeps reading the
size of its own video window, which the new window does not touch. The new
window holds the two views side by side at the resolution they have, is
resized with them, and is declared with stereo_declare_x11_child()
(libstereo-declare 1.7.0) on the nearest ancestor the window manager
manages (it carries WM_STATE, ICCCM 4.1.3.1), with the size one view is shown
at, the video window's size (support version 8, CHILD-PLACE.md). The window
selects no events, so the pointer and the keys go on to the video window.
Stereo KWin resizes each view once, into the video window's rectangle. When
the video output closes, which is also when a 3D video gives way to a 2D one
in the same window, the declaration is taken back with
stereo_remove_x11_child() and the window destroyed.

Where the desktop announces support version 5 to 7, the video window is
declared as the child with one view in each half of it, as before, and VLC
says so: a message in its log and the dialog "3D video shown at reduced
width". Below 5, or when the declaration fails, the dialog is "3D video shown
flat" and the log says why, instead of one view shown as if it worked. The
Wayland path says the same when its declaration fails.

A video window that the window manager manages itself (VLC without the Qt
interface's embedded video) keeps stereo_declare_x11() and
stereo_remove_x11(): the compositor makes such a window hold both views.
Xlib errors from windows that are already gone are ignored for these calls
only.

Nothing in VLC upstream declares stereo windows; the change is for VLC
Stereo only.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
